---
description: Follow the Seattle Deckbuilder architecture on every change
alwaysApply: true
---

Before changing this project, read README.md at the repo root and follow it.

- Game rules live in `src/game` and must stay headless. Do not import React, CSS, or PeerJS from the engine.
- Change game state only by sending commands through the session. Do not mutate state from components.
- Animate only from the visual event queue in `src/visual/queue.js`, using `await sleep(ms)`. `Card` takes `flip` for a 3D turn that shows the card back. The queue sets it when a card is drawn or fills the trade row. Discarded and bought cards fly to the center and shrink for that wait. Row slots slide when their position changes.
- Every card definition lives in `src/cards.js`. Render cards only with `src/components/Card.jsx`.
- Multiplayer goes through PeerJS in `src/net/session.js`. The host applies commands and sends each player a redacted view.
- The game is phone-first. Lay screens out with absolute divs in `src/index.css` on the 390×740 board.
- When the architecture changes, update README.md in the same change.
